WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:03.790
Now we're going to talk about animation editors

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.669
and features within the engine.

3
00:00:05.669 --> 00:00:08.750
There are several animation editors or sub-editors,

4
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.630
as we like to call them, within the engine.

5
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.669
I'm just going to give you a quick overview of those,

6
00:00:12.669 --> 00:00:14.349
and then once we get into the engine,

7
00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:16.309
we'll explore it a little bit more depth.

8
00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:19.070
We have the animation blend space editor,

9
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:22.070
which is a great way to control your animations,

10
00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:23.629
especially your real-time animations,

11
00:00:23.629 --> 00:00:25.390
have them set up in order to,

12
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.149
let's say, blend several different types

13
00:00:27.149 --> 00:00:29.149
of animations like a walk to a lean,

14
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.690
a lean to a right lean, a left lean,

15
00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.609
perhaps lean back as they're walking.

16
00:00:33.609 --> 00:00:35.840
This is where you would do that.

17
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.520
Now the animation blueprint editor,

18
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.280
we won't be diving into that too much,

19
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.240
but that is where you can set up

20
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.679
very specific animation blueprints,

21
00:00:43.679 --> 00:00:45.240
as the name does state,

22
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.939
to set up various effects and how things can happen.

23
00:00:47.939 --> 00:00:50.079
This is where you could put a live link

24
00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:52.399
through your control rig, many powerful things,

25
00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:55.899
and it works very much like our blueprint editor itself

26
00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:57.340
within the engine.

27
00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.240
Then we have the animation sequence editor,

28
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.759
which is where you can take some existing animations

29
00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:04.980
and add more curves to it, make some notifications.

30
00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.819
And we will explore this one just a little bit

31
00:01:06.819 --> 00:01:09.420
to create our own little custom animation.

32
00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.340
Now there's a new thing with the animation mode

33
00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.060
that is activated when you have a control rig

34
00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:14.980
within your scene.

35
00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:17.219
So you will need a control rig to activate it.

36
00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:19.060
You can pull it up, but you won't be able to use it

37
00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.900
unless there's an active control rig in your scene.

38
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.939
So some of the things you'll see is the poses,

39
00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:26.540
tweens, snapper, trails, and even a pivot.

40
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.019
So you can customize your pivot.

41
00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.480
These are all very powerful,

42
00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.319
and I've included a link as well that you can reference

43
00:01:32.319 --> 00:01:36.239
to further learn about these really powerful tools

44
00:01:36.239 --> 00:01:38.620
that have been added within the engine.
